 13194139535280 true] [17592186341373 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341378 13194139535280 true] [17592186341373 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535280 true] [17592186341373 1041 "selection" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341373 1104 #edb/ref 17592186341374 13194139535280 true] [17592186341373 1110 #uuid "bf05e959-ea8c-5cf6-bfd2-0d4d678cf741" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341374 1034 "x{y}^{″}+(x+1){y}^{′}-y=0" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341374 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535280 true] [17592186341374 1111 #uuid "f707b7b8-ab16-55a2-8396-6c0d6a5362d9" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341375 1034 "x{y}^{″}+(x+1){y}^{′}=0" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341375 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535280 true] [17592186341375 1111 #uuid "74f85049-fd80-5f31-8912-242efdd76111" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341376 1034 "x{y}^{″}+x{y}^{′}-y=0" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341376 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535280 true] [17592186341376 1111 #uuid "2cbdae09-107a-5ccc-9c79-1d465c9a5378" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341377 1034 "{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-y={e}^{x}" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341377 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535280 true] [17592186341377 1111 #uuid "d5594ba2-072f-5ae5-bd34-3bc5718aada8" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341378 1034 "{y}^{″}+\\frac{x+1}{x}{y}^{′}-y={e}^{x}" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341378 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535280 true] [17592186341378 1111 #uuid "1184f437-b848-5bf7-a89a-2ac02dd56283" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341379 1017 #edb/ref 17592186341380 13194139535280 true] [17592186341379 1089 "q-131001" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341379 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535280 true] [17592186341379 1100 "Which of the following systems is an initial value problem?\n\n- ${y}^{″}-{x}^{2}{y}^{′}+y=x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=2$\n- ${y}^{″}+{y}^{′}+y=1,\\,y(\\pi )=1,\\,{y}^{′}(\\pi )=2$\n- ${y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-y=x{e}^{x}$" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341379 1113 #uuid "5d885e48-2e79-58d6-9707-a6c9e1d542f5" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341379 1145 "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not an initial value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$ and $x=2$). This is a **boundary value problem.**\n\n- The second system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=\\pi $).\n\n- The third system is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified." 13194139535280 true] [17592186341380 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341381 13194139535280 true] [17592186341380 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341382 13194139535280 true] [17592186341380 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341383 13194139535280 true] [17592186341380 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341384 13194139535280 true] [17592186341380 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341385 13194139535280 true] [17592186341380 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535280 true] [17592186341380 1041 "selection" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341380 1104 #edb/ref 17592186341385 13194139535280 true] [17592186341380 1110 #uuid "f97b2fa5-35c7-528d-8346-6234742f1220" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341381 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341381 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535280 true] [17592186341381 1111 #uuid "fb98d297-b305-5b1f-aabb-31785113c708" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341382 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341382 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535280 true] [17592186341382 1111 #uuid "7005190e-e172-58bd-986b-51724efb5d90" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341383 1034 "I only" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341383 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535280 true] [17592186341383 1111 #uuid "1d3f2c93-6a05-50d5-bb43-35203c048ef0" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341384 1034 "I and II only" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341384 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535280 true] [17592186341384 1111 #uuid "628c02e9-e153-5d65-8232-75b1538b6bc7" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341385 1034 "II only" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341385 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535280 true] [17592186341385 1111 #uuid "ec4604f3-de94-5e52-b7d6-ef5649b76ca7" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341386 1017 #edb/ref 17592186341387 13194139535280 true] [17592186341386 1017 #edb/ref 17592186341390 13194139535280 true] [17592186341386 1017 #edb/ref 17592186341393 13194139535280 true] [17592186341386 1089 "q-337996" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341386 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535280 true] [17592186341386 1100 "Determine which of the following second-order ODEs are homogeneous, and which are inhomogeneous.\n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+6y=7$ is {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x){y}^{″}+(1-x){y}^{′}-4y=0$ is {{field-2}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}+xy+{x}^{3}=0$ is {{field-3}}." 13194139535280 true] [17592186341386 1113 #uuid "7fc00c12-63c8-559a-aa45-1b909350bd43" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341386 1145 "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+5{y}^{′}+6y=7\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=7,$ which is different from zero.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x){y}^{″}+(1-x){y}^{′}-4y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+xy+{x}^{3}=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+xy=-{x}^{