79dba891-0fd5-5b33-acae-cf1ca4fcb237" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341423 1145 "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not an initial value problem. It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=0$ and $x=2$). This is a **boundary value problem.**\n\n- The second system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$).\n\n- The third system is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified." 13194139535280 true] [17592186341424 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341425 13194139535280 true] [17592186341424 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341426 13194139535280 true] [17592186341424 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341427 13194139535280 true] [17592186341424 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341428 13194139535280 true] [17592186341424 1000 #edb/ref 17592186341429 13194139535280 true] [17592186341424 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535280 true] [17592186341424 1041 "selection" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341424 1104 #edb/ref 17592186341429 13194139535280 true] [17592186341424 1110 #uuid "e8bb9631-31f8-57b4-8dbf-afa49adc64d6" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341425 1034 "II and III only" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341425 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535280 true] [17592186341425 1111 #uuid "549a6203-d92c-550d-a36f-ac104a959412" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341426 1034 "I and III only" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341426 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535280 true] [17592186341426 1111 #uuid "4235cb7f-d7df-51e9-8750-f84e61256173" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341427 1034 "I only" 13194139535280 true] [17592186341427 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139535280 true